    {
      "post_id": "86357",
      "author_handle": "thash1979",
      "date_as_displayed": "Posted 10 years 8 months ago",
      "body": "I nursed my son the whole time I was pregnant with my daughter. My son, at the time was around 18 months when my daughter was born. I ended up stopping around the two weeks before I gave birth to my daughter. Just because I did not want to be nursing both at the same time. I didn't have any problems with having enough milk for him the time I was nursing and pregnant. I had no problems when my daughter being born and having a milk supply ready for her. I didn't' have that tenderness of my breasts when the milk came in or tender nipples. It was easier doing it this way, than if I would have stopped and then had to start having so many months in between them.",
      "permalink": "https://www.justparents.co.uk/forums/topic-4501/#86357",
